    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="1259" n="1109" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg1109"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister of the
                        Netherlands.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-04-18"><hi rendition="#italic">April 18,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 130.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 10th instant, by which, in accordance with instructions you
                    have received from your Government, the Government of the United States <pb
                        facs="1260" n="1110" xml:id="pg1110"/> is invited to be officially
                    represented by delegates at the Second Peace Conference which is to convene at
                    The Hague on the 15th of June next.</p>
                <p>I beg you to be so good as to inform your Government that the Government of the
                    United States accepts the invitation with great pleasure, and that it will at an
                    early date communicate the names of its delegates.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
